rocess  and the police come in and she's sitting  against the door thinking of that video  of kevin  and it cuts to black and the episode  ends there  so rest in peace colin and mr potts  they both look pretty dead after last  week's recap  and the follow-up video on the trailer  breakdown and theories  i had a lot of comments starting to  wonder if colin might be  a suspect where things are left i think  that's probably not the case  i think we found out his dirty little  secret and we didn't learn much about mr  potts but it does seem like he was  operating on his own  and that his intention was just to use  these girls as sex slaves  at the end we do get closure for the  katy bailey case  we should see her reunited with dawn and  kenzie mayor continuing to work the case  was the difference in seeing this thing  through and there was a price  detective colin zabal looks like he paid  it with his life  overall this was one of the most  gripping endings of an episode in the  series  they did a solid job in setting up the  pieces to make things  incredibly intense in the face-off  inside benny's tavern  even after picking through the trailer  for clues i really wasn't sure if they  were gonna be where the girls were being  held when it all went down  as it played out losing colin was like  having the wind knocked out of you  the fact that he fumbled his way through  their date and still couldn't let go of  his ideas about mayor  it all worked really well if nothing  else it's going to have an impact on  mayor going forward and she's already  got a lot of  other regrets and pain that is all  competing for her attention  you feel for mayor and i thought most of  this was handled well  but from my perspective there's still  this yeah that's awful  but energy in her story i like mare and  most of her backstory  is super compelling i mean not only did  her father commit suicide when she was a  teen  but her son followed in his footsteps of  course i like a flawed character but the  power dynamic between her and  carrie is so skewed that it's still hard  to accept how things played out  plus she doesn't seem to have any  remorse about doing what she did  and everyone that knows about it seems  willing to write it off as yeah that's  just mare  but the story isn't told yet so we'll  see where they go  with the kidnapper out of the way the  path is cleared to get to the bottom of  aaron's story  who is dj's father who killed her and  essentially what do these things say  about the town of easttown  in an episode where we got some answers  things also took  some unexpected turns and as i mentioned  at the beginning our understanding of  the developments is incomplete  if i hadn't watched the trailer the  dylan ingesting would have been a  complete surprise  and i was shocked when brianna said that  he left the house on the night aaron  died  the ross family and the deacon mark  reveals were a little more telegraphed  but it still isn't clear how things are  gonna play out the pace is still full  speed ahead  the answer to new mysteries ratio isn't  getting too lopsided which is nice  and there are still some funny moments  to lighten things up from time to time  most of those belong to jean smart and  this episode was no exception  i really loved her face as she was  grabbing food as mr carroll was coming  clean about their affair  she also had a very human moment when  she was with carrie  telling her that she was helping her for  purely selfish reasons  because she's afraid carrie's gonna get  full custody and cut them  out of drew's life and she can't bear to  lose another one  the spotlight being on the rosses also  makes me wonder about faye and frank  having problems  sure she would have been mad at him  because of what happened with mare  coming over to their house  but they're having ongoing problems  hints that there may have been  other suspicions or something else going  on before that happened  lori caught a lot of my attention i know  she had the underlying tension with jon  going on but it seemed like she was  really kind of  nudging mare to maybe pay attention to  her husband  an old weird cousin billy on top of that  they're obvious suspects that were  flying under the radar because they were  the somewhat normal hometown types  they seem mostly like good guys but lori  is in a unique position to know things  about them that nobody else does  i'll get into all of that more in the  follow-up video the trailer this week  isn't quite as juicy so we'll be able to  get through that pretty quick and focus  on  end game theories that'll come out in a  few days  for now there's a lot to think about rip  rip  to betty carroll and colin zabel let me  know in the comments what you think  about the episode what you think about  that  ending and where you think things are  going from here  please like this video if you enjoyed it  please subscribe to my channel if you  haven't already  thanks for watching i'll talk to you  soon
 

